  "id": "dopa",
  "term": "dopa",
  "definition": "In this packet, DOPA refers to L-DOPA, a chemical precursor of dopamine used in dopamine replacement therapy for Parkinson’s disease. It is used to help reduce motor problems related to loss or dysfunction of dopamine neurons, but it can also produce treatment-related involuntary movements known as L-DOPA-induced dyskinesias.",
